# K03 NS-ROLES-2 (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-2-20261007-20; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#resolved-head-consumption,
# #declaration-visibility): a named Structure's body takes the common roles of the root and a method.
# Later is defined below Host: in Host's body it is unknown (an ordinary named Structure is visible from its place
# on), so `b: Later` defines b with the free name Later -- no binding; a write of b's v names no field of b: refused.
Host:
    b: Later
end: Host
Later:
    int: v 1
end: Later
fn: m () int
    Host\b\v: 5
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
